7.	Python Program using socket — Simple Port Scanner


Source Code:
import socket

target = "127.0.0.1" #localhost
ports = [21,22, 80, 443]

for port in ports:
    s = socket.socket()
    result = s.connect_ex((target, port))
    if result == 0:
        print(f"Port {port} is OPEN") 

    else: 
        print(f"Port {port} is CLOSED")

    s.close()






8.	Program to generate hash values of a string using hashlib library.

Source Code:

import hashlib

text = "CyberSecurity123"

# MD5 Hash
md5_hash = hashlib.md5(text.encode())
print("MD5 Hash:", md5_hash.hexdigest())

# SHA1 Hash
